# The pocket pager: a pocket computer running pager, two turtles
# running turtleagent and a base computer. At 4 s the base computer
# starts a mine line on turtle 2, which has fuel for only a few
# blocks, so it raises a fuel alert. At 12 s the base computer raises
# an alert of its own through the bus.
name Pager
description A pocket computer (10) running pager, two turtles running turtleagent and a base computer (5).
description At 4 s the base computer starts a mine line on turtle 2, which soon runs out of fuel; at 12 s it raises a power alert of its own.
description Touch an alert on the pager for details and Acknowledge; the Turtles tab is a small fleet view.

ground -8 -8 8 8 0 4 ores=false pockets=false

turtle 1 label=Miner
  pos -2 0 1
  heading north
  fuel 900
  slots coal*8
  peripheral left modem
  autorun turtleagent

turtle 2 label=Digger
  pos 2 0 1
  heading north
  fuel 6
  peripheral left modem
  autorun turtleagent

computer 5 label=Base
  pos 0 -3 1
  peripheral top modem

pocket 10 label=Pager
  peripheral back modem
  autorun pager

at 4 type 5 turtlejob 2 mineline 20 false 10 false
at 12 type 5 alert power Smelter out of power

# The pager lists both alerts, the newest (the base's) first, and has
# heard both turtles.
check pager shows the turtle and base alerts
  seconds 25
  expect screen 10 Base    power Smelter
  expect screen 10 Digger  fuel  out of f
  expect screen 10 2 alerts, 2 new, 2 turtles
  expect screen 5 OK: mineline starting
  expect turtle 2 fuel = 0
  expect no-error
